--- (4d) FINITE-CHECK feasibility ---
  For V > V* the lemma gives #good>0 RIGOROUSLY. For V <= V* a FINITE check suffices.
  Dilation (THM-531): a cluster d*{0,1,..} reduces to the base {0,1,..} (gcd=1),
  so the cluster-offset pattern is WLOG primitive; #patterns of bounded spread is finite.
  The small part P ranges over the 2^13-1 nonempty subsets of [1,13] (finite).
  => the finite check is over {primitive cluster patterns} x {P-subsets} x {V<=V*},
     each an EXACT-rational M(S) evaluation. Feasible (V* <= few hundred).

